      {
        "id": 156281,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-28T04:14:38.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Minty fresh! Ra did most of the heavy lifting, with AA getting him extra power uses and a very timely play of Scorched Earth that sent the Ennead reeling. Nuit went down first, then Set. Incapped Set may be runner up for MVP, given the cards he helped my team pull out. (Inferno in particular was well-timed). The environment was mostly a non-issue, aside from giving Scholar a 2 HP healing power instead of 1 HP.</p><p>Fanatic, sad to say, didn't do much besides damage. I never use Sacrosanct Martyr in the first place, there was never a target at or under 4 HP at the start of her turn so the three Final Dives she pulled were useless.</p><p>Ended with everyone between mid teens and mid 20s, thanks in part to AA's healing vibes.</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
        "post_type": 1,
