      {
        "id": 156282,
        "name": "bessyrocks12",
        "username": "bessyrocks12",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bessyrocks12/{size}/2447_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-28T05:37:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint in one of the closest games I've ever played. Took out Nuit and Shu first, but the damage started to catch up. Ra was dominating, but lots of swinging HP. Luckily, only one extra member came out. Last god was down to 13, but I was down to 1 HP with both Scholar and Fanatic, and it looked like a loss. However, I pulled out Aegis and used Sancrosect Martyr for 5 damage. Aegis protected me from the (overkill), Annubis reacted to the card being destroyed and hit her for two, but Fanatic still with 8. Scholar uses Know When to Turn Loose for 5 damage, bringing them down to 3. Scholar healed to 2 HP. The environment cleaned up with a hit for 4, winning me the game. Going from a total of 2 HP to 10 while the villain dropped from 14 to -1 was a unforseen win.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:36:00.632Z",
